{"id": "EUVD-2026-93317", "enisaUuid": "2d64a592-aca5-332b-b6f2-edcdff6d4965", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: only operate on TDLS peers in the TDLS code\n\nieee80211_tdls_oper() can operate on the AP station, which then\nyields various warnings when the AP station is removed then or\nat a later point in time after being confused for a TDLS peer.\n\nAlways check that the station is a TDLS peer.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:43", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0cd452ccaa5c5971440256ce72c64611eca176c1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6f0a100df8539ce90f37c14e1945f396ca2410bc"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5v23-w7xx-382w", "CVE-2026-98332"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d3a8652-b701-39c7-9ecf-dc8447bdb6c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "747e713c-09a2-32f4-a67a-ea6f4197ff9b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dfe018bf99537e42c816d3f543620a7e09fcf3cd <0cd452ccaa5c5971440256ce72c64611eca176c1"}, {"id": "c3daee03-86c3-35f0-9846-8d239f46965f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "ce3b86da-7943-3a6b-a8ea-9ca4ca4772fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.2"}, {"id": "e83ae8b2-65c5-3f61-a06f-9c0a4cf95226", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "f57ab9af-2375-3d60-8179-8df7e89e6055", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dfe018bf99537e42c816d3f543620a7e09fcf3cd <6f0a100df8539ce90f37c14e1945f396ca2410bc"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "13012946-e2c6-33ec-aab0-023ff5eccbc2", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}